        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Northwest uses the Fixed Asset Method to report storage.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">This account captures storage encroachments on Northwest&#8217;s fixed asset system balancing gas recorded in account 117.2. Northwest debits 808.1 and credits 117.4 for any net shortage of supplied gas and debits 117.4 and credits 808.2 for any net excess of supplied gas.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The gas inventory balance is classified to account 164.1. Gas is withdrawn from this account for expansion projects and to replace gas lost or used during maintenance work.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
