      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Depreciation Incremental-various based on contract life (RP22-1155) negative salvage 0.20% (RP22-1155) and range from 3.15% to 10.20%. All transmission plant depreciation was computed on depreciable plant in service based on the balance at the end of the preceding month.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline">General Plant</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">General plant depreciation rates range from 4.00% to 33.33% (RP22-1155) based on the expected service life. General plant depreciation was primarily computed on depreciable plant in service based on the balance at the end of the preceding month.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline">Other Storage</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Depreciation 1.45% (RP22-1155) Negative Salvage 0.15% (RP22-1155)</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">All other storage plant depreciation was computed on depreciable plant in service based on the balance at the end of the preceding month.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline">Underground Storage</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Depreciation 2.23% (RP22-1155) Negative Salvage 0.53% (RP22-1155)</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">All underground storage plant depreciation was computed on depreciable plant in service based on the balance at the end of the preceding month.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-34" id="fn-34" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline">Transmission Onshore</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Depreciation Incremental-various based on contract life (RP22-1155) negative salvage 0.20% (RP22-1155) and range from 3.15% to 10.20%. All transmission plant depreciation was computed on depreciable plant in service based on the balance at the end of the preceding month.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-35" id="fn-35" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline">General Plant</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">General plant depreciation rates range from 4.00% to 33.33% (RP22-1155) based on the expected service life. General plant depreciation was primarily computed on depreciable plant in service based on the balance at the end of the preceding month.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-36" id="fn-36" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline">Other Storage</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Depreciation 1.45% (RP22-1155) Negative Salvage 0.15% (RP22-1155)</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">All other storage plant depreciation was computed on depreciable plant in service based on the balance at the end of the preceding month.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-37" id="fn-37" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">LETTER OF CREDIT FEES INCURRED BY WILLIAMS ARE CHARGED TO ITS SUBSIDIARIES, INCLUDING NORTHWEST PIPELINE BASED ON A THREE-FACTOR FORMULA, WHICH CONSIDERS REVENUES; PROPERTY, PLANT AND EQUIPMENT; AND PAYROLL</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-38" id="fn-38" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-bottom:1pt;margin-top:15pt">
        <table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%">
          <tr>
            <td style="width:1.0%"/>
            <td style="width:98.900%"/>
            <td style="width:0.1%"/>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000;border-left:1pt solid #000;border-right:1pt solid #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom">
              <div>
                <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:115%">Schedule Page: 358 Line No.: 6 Column: (d)</span>
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Enterprise shared services are charged to Northwest and other franchises via specific allocations based on a relationship with the delivery of services, as in the case of some human resource services costs are allocated based on employee headcount, or via general allocations using the modified Massachusetts formula for residual overhead costs that are not readily assignable to a particular operating area or franchise via specific allocation.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-39" id="fn-39" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-bottom:1pt;margin-top:15pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Enterprise shared services are charged to Northwest and other franchises for fleet leasing and other fleet costs via specific allocations based on labor costs assigned to capital work orders.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-40" id="fn-40" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:15pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Payroll and non-payroll charges for the benefit of the Transmission &amp; Gulf of America Operating Area that are not specific to a franchise are allocated to franchises included in the Transmission &amp; Gulf of America Operating Area, including Northwest, via specific allocations based on a relationship with the delivery of services, as in the case of some human resource services costs are allocated based on employee headcount, or via general allocations using the modified Massachusetts formula for residual overhead costs that are not readily assignable to a particular franchise via specific allocation. The Transmission &amp; Gulf of America Operating Area includes certain non-regulated franchises, MountainWest Overthrust Pipeline, LLC, MountainWest Pipeline, LLC, Northwest Pipeline LLC, and Transcontinental Gas Pipe Line Company, LLC. Allocation to Williams Partners Operating LLC is for the non-regulated franchises in the operating area.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-41" id="fn-41" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-bottom:1pt;margin-top:15pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Storage facilities charges recorded to a specific work order for the benefit of the Transmission &amp; Gulf of America Operating Area that are not specific to a franchise are allocated to franchises included in the Transmission &amp; Gulf of America Operating Area, including Northwest, via specific allocations. The Transmission &amp; Gulf of America Operating Area includes certain non-regulated franchises, MountainWest Overthrust Pipeline, LLC, MountainWest Pipeline, LLC, Northwest Pipeline LLC, and Transcontinental Gas Pipe Line Company, LLC.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-42" id="fn-42" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:10pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Houston, Texas Williams tower building rent is allocated based on employee labor costs.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-43" id="fn-43" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:10pt;text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Employees' direct assignment payroll and non-payroll charges for the benefit of the Transmission &amp; Gulf of America Operating Area that are not specific to a franchise are allocated to franchises included in the Transmission &amp; Gulf of America Operating Area based on the modified Massachusetts formula. The Transmission</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:10pt;text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">&amp; Gulf of America Operating Area includes certain non-regulated franchises, MountainWest Overthrust Pipeline, LLC, MountainWest Pipeline, LLC, Northwest Pipeline LLC, and Transcontinental Gas Pipe Line Company, LLC.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-44" id="fn-44" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Salt Lake City, Utah building rent is allocated based on employee labor costs.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-45" id="fn-45" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">JACKSON PRAIRIE IS JOINTLY OWNED BY THREE COMPANIES: NORTHWEST (RESPONDENT), PUGET SOUND ENERGY AND AVISTA CORPORATION, EACH OWNS ONE THIRD OF THE FACILITIES.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-46" id="fn-46" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">COSTS REPRESENTS RESPONDENT'S 22.3% SHARE OF FACILITIES. TRANSWESTERN PIPELINE OWNS THE REMAINING 77.7%.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-47" id="fn-47" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Reflects the change in system storage used for system balancing.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-48" id="fn-48" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Reflects the change in system storage used for system balancing.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-49" id="fn-49" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">The Transferred to Tanks and "Boil Off" Vaporization Loss volumes do not include regeneration gas.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-50" id="fn-50" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">The Transferred to Tanks and "Boil Off" Vaporization Loss volumes do not include regeneration gas.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-51" id="fn-51" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Owned 100% by the town of Rangely, Colorado.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-52" id="fn-52" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Owned 50.15% by EPCOR Utilities, Inc., and 49.85% by Puget Sound Energy, Inc.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-53" id="fn-53" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Colorado Section: Originally, 22.3% ownership by Northwest Pipeline LLC (Respondent) and 77.7% by Transwestern (Operator).</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-54" id="fn-54" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">New Mexico Section: Originally, 22.3% ownership by Northwest Pipeline LLC (Respondent) and 77.7% by Transwestern (Operator).</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-55" id="fn-55" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Single day peak is scheduled peak day.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-56" id="fn-56" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">The Other Operational Activities relates to the OBA imbalances at receipt and delivery points associated with interstate pipelines. These quantities cannot be tied directly to the gas that is withdrawn from storage or that is taken out or put into line pack.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-57" id="fn-57" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Consecutive three-day peak is scheduled peak days.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-58" id="fn-58" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">The Other Operational Activities relates to the OBA imbalances at receipt and delivery points associated with interstate pipelines. These quantities cannot be tied directly to the gas that is withdrawn from storage or that is taken out or put into line pack.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-59" id="fn-59" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:12pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%;text-decoration:underline">Adjustment for ACA Purposes:</span>
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">The volumes in column (c) include volumes received from storage and transported under Northwest&#8217;s TF-2 Firm Redelivery Transportation service and other firm and interruptible transportation services to redeliver gas stored in (1) the Jackson Prairie Storage Project under Rate Schedules SGS-2F, SGS-2I or PAL, and (2) the Plymouth LNG Facility under Rate Schedules LS-2F or LS-2I. Northwest assesses the ACA surcharge on all transportation volumes that are delivered into the Jackson Prairie Storage Project and the Plymouth LNG Facility. Consequently, the ACA surcharge should not be assessed on volumes a second time when they move out of storage. The (1) TF-2 Redelivery Transportation volumes reported on Page 305, Line 4, Column (j) and (2) other 2024 firm and interruptible transportation volumes of 40,564,578 Dth redelivered from the Jackson Prairie Storage Project and the Plymouth LNG Facility should be excluded for ACA billing purposes from the volumes reported on Page 520, Line No. 5, Column (c). The ACA volume that should be used for ACA billing purposes is 924,758,501 Dth (i.e., 924,758,501 Dth (Total Dekatherms, page 305 column j) - 8,592,077 Dth (TF-2, page 305 column j, line 4) - 31,972,501 Dth (TF-1 Storage Re-deliveries transported from storage).</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-60" id="fn-60" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Gas of Others Received for Transmission represents scheduled receipt nominations net of in-kind fuel. The volumes shown do not impact the overall page 520 system gas balance because the differences between scheduled receipt nominations and actual physical receipts are captured in the 806 imbalances and are included in the numbers shown on lines 10 and 25 of page 520. The in-kind reimbursements are shown on lines 13 and 14.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-61" id="fn-61" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Gas of Others Received for Contract Storage represents scheduled withdrawal nominations by others as shown on page 307. The volumes shown do not impact the overall page 520 system gas balance because the differences between scheduled storage withdrawal nominations and actual physical storage receipts onto the mainline are captured in the 806 imbalances shown on lines 10 and 25.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:12pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Northwest had the following storage quantities at 12/31/2024:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:12pt">
        <table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:48.660%">
          <tr>
            <td style="width:1.0%"/>
            <td style="width:55.169%"/>
            <td style="width:0.1%"/>
            <td style="width:1.0%"/>
            <td style="width:42.631%"/>
            <td style="width:0.1%"/>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/>
            <td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:center;text-indent:23pt;vertical-align:top">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%;text-decoration:underline">Dth</span>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <div>
                <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Jackson Prairie Storage</span>
              </div>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/>
          </tr>
