    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-63" id="fn-63" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Gas Received as Imbalances reflects the gas recorded (Northwest&#8217;s imbalances are cleared through in-kind exchanges and reflects the net change) in account 806 that relates to OBA, Receiving Party, Shipper and Park and Loan imbalances and is shown as Gas Received from others on page 328, lines 1-4 column (c).</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-64" id="fn-64" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Gas Received as Imbalances reflects the gas recorded (Northwest&#8217;s imbalances are cleared through in-kind exchanges and reflects the net change) in account 806 that relates to OBA, Receiving Party, Shipper and Park and Loan imbalances and is shown as Gas Received from others on page 328, lines 1-4 column (c).</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-65" id="fn-65" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Other Gas Withdrawn from Storage relates to system balancing.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-66" id="fn-66" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Other Gas Withdrawn from Storage relates to system balancing.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-67" id="fn-67" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Northwest books its fuel usage, reimbursements and imbalance activity on a month lag. However, at year end Northwest also books the actual December activity. Therefore, the first quarter of the year will only contain two months of activity and the fourth quarter of the year will contain four months of activity so that the year-to-date numbers reflect 12 months of activity.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-68" id="fn-68" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">See footnote on line 13, col. (c). Because of this procedure, the "Current 3 Months&#8221; column includes four months of activity in order to conform to Northwest&#8217;s books.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-69" id="fn-69" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Deliveries of Gas Transported by Others represents scheduled delivery nominations. The volumes shown do not impact the overall page 520 system gas balance because the differences between scheduled delivery</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">nominations and actual physical deliveries are captured in the 806 imbalances and are included in the numbers shown on lines 10 and 25 of page 520.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-70" id="fn-70" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Deliveries of Gas Transported by Others represents scheduled delivery nominations. The volumes shown do not impact the overall page 520 system gas balance because the differences between scheduled delivery nominations and actual physical deliveries are captured in the 806 imbalances and are included in the numbers shown on lines 10 and 25 of page 520.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-71" id="fn-71" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Deliveries of Contract Storage Gas represents scheduled injection nominations by others as shown on page 307. The volumes shown do not impact the overall page 520 system gas balance because the difference between scheduled storage injections nominations and actual physical volumes delivered into storage are captured in the 806 imbalances shown on lines 10 and 25.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-72" id="fn-72" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Deliveries of Contract Storage Gas represents scheduled injection nominations by others as shown on page 307. The volumes shown do not impact the overall page 520 system gas balance because the difference between scheduled storage injections nominations and actual physical volumes delivered into storage are captured in the 806 imbalances shown on lines 10 and 25.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-73" id="fn-73" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Gas Delivered as Imbalances reflects the gas recorded in account 806 that relates to OBA, Receiving Party, Shipper and Park and Loan imbalances and is shown as Gas Delivered to Others on page 328, lines 1-4 column (e).</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-74" id="fn-74" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Gas Delivered as Imbalances reflects the gas recorded in account 806 that relates to OBA, Receiving Party, Shipper and Park and Loan imbalances and is shown as Gas Delivered to Others on page 328, lines 1-4 column (e).</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-75" id="fn-75" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Other Gas Delivered to Storage relates to system balancing.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-76" id="fn-76" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Other Gas Delivered to Storage relates to system balancing.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-77" id="fn-77" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Northwest books its fuel usage, reimbursements and imbalance activity on a month lag. However, at year end Northwest also books the actual December activity. Therefore, the first quarter of the year will only contain two months of activity and the fourth quarter of 6the year will contain four months of activity so that the year-to-date numbers reflect 12 months of activity.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-78" id="fn-78" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">See footnote on line 28, col. (c). Because of this procedure, the &#8220;Current 3 Months&#8221; column includes four months of activity in order to conform to Northwest&#8217;s books.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-79" id="fn-79" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">The Other Deliveries reflects gas used for purposes other than operating compressor stations as reported on page 331, plus working gas, change in line pack and gas used in other non-mainline projects.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-80" id="fn-80" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">The Other Deliveries reflects gas used for purposes other than operating compressor stations as reported on page 331, plus working gas, change in line pack and gas used in other non-mainline projects.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-81" id="fn-81" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">The numbers shown on this page include any fuel usage and in-kind reimbursements associated with transmission and storage rate schedules.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:12pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Northwest records its fuel usage, reimbursements and imbalance activity on a month-lag. However, at year end Northwest also records the actual December activity. Therefore, the first quarter of the year will only contain two months of activity and the fourth quarter of the year will contain four months of activity so that the year-to-date numbers reflect 12 months of activity. Therefore, the &#8220;Month 3&#8221; columns include two months of activity in order to conform to Northwest&#8217;s books.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-82" id="fn-82" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">The numbers shown on this page are derived by taking the total volume of throughput and allocating it among the three contract categories (i.e. contracts with discounted rates, contracts with negotiated rates, and contracts with recourse rates) based on the percentage of gas transported for each contract type.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-83" id="fn-83" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Northwest does not discount fuel.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-84" id="fn-84" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:5pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Any monthly excess or deficiency of gas is refunded or collected in-kind through Northwest&#8217;s semi-annual fuel filing process.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
